        'short' => 'Cleaning supply and return ductwork when there is visible debris, pest activity, mold growth, or construction dust.',
        'hero_heading' => 'Air duct cleaning',
        'hero_text' => 'Get connected with an independent provider who can inspect your ductwork and clean it when it is actually needed.',
        'overview' => '<p>Air ducts carry every cubic foot of air your system heats or cools. Over time they collect dust, and after renovations, pest problems, or water damage they can collect much worse. The U.S. Environmental Protection Agency suggests duct cleaning when there is substantial visible mold growth, evidence of rodents or insects, or ducts clogged with dust and debris that is being released into the home.</p><p>Professional cleaning uses powerful negative-pressure vacuums and brushes or air whips to dislodge debris throughout the system — including the blower, coils, and drain pan when they are part of the job. Duct cleaning is not a cure-all for allergies, so it should be done for a clear reason.</p>',
