        'image' => 'smart-thermostat.jpg',
        'featured' => false,
        'short' => 'Filtration, humidity control, ventilation, and air purification that work with your HVAC system.',
        'hero_heading' => 'Indoor air quality solutions',
        'hero_text' => 'Dust, humidity, odors, and stale air can often be improved through your HVAC system. Get connected with a provider who can help.',
        'overview' => '<p>Your heating and cooling system moves the air in your home many times a day, which makes it the most practical place to improve air quality for the whole house. Upgrades fall into four groups: <strong>filtration</strong> (capturing particles), <strong>humidity control</strong> (adding or removing moisture), <strong>ventilation</strong> (bringing in fresh air), and <strong>air cleaning</strong> (UV lights and other technologies aimed at specific problems).</p><p>The best approach starts with the symptom — dry winter air, summer clamminess, dust, odors, or stuffiness — and targets the cause rather than adding equipment for its own sake.</p>',
        'problems' => [
            ['title' => 'Too humid', 'text' => 'Clammy air, condensation on windows, and musty smells suggest excess moisture.'],
            ['title' => 'Too dry', 'text' => 'Static shocks, dry skin, and cracking wood floors are common in heated winter air.'],
            ['title' => 'Dust and allergens', 'text' => 'Basic filters catch large particles but let fine dust, pollen, and pet dander through.'],
            ['title' => 'Stale air', 'text' => 'Tightly sealed modern homes can build up odors and indoor pollutants without ventilation.'],
        ],
        'options' => [
            ['title' => 'Upgraded filtration', 'text' => 'MERV 11–13 media filters in a deep filter cabinet, matched to what your blower can handle.'],
            ['title' => 'Whole-home humidifiers and dehumidifiers', 'text' => 'Maintain indoor humidity in a comfortable range of roughly 30–50%.'],
            ['title' => 'ERV and HRV ventilation', 'text' => 'Bring in fresh outdoor air while recovering much of the heating or cooling energy.'],
