            'Allergy or asthma symptoms are worse indoors',
            'Rooms feel stuffy, and odors linger after cooking',
        ],
        'details' => '<h2>A note on filter ratings</h2><p>Higher MERV ratings capture smaller particles but can also restrict airflow if the system was not designed for them. A provider can check static pressure and recommend a filter or filter cabinet that improves air quality without straining the blower.</p>',
        'faqs' => [
            ['question' => 'What indoor humidity level is best?', 'answer' => 'Roughly 30–50% relative humidity is comfortable for most people and helps limit dust mites and mold. In very cold weather, aim for the lower end to avoid window condensation.'],
            ['question' => 'What MERV filter should I use?', 'answer' => 'Many residential systems work well with MERV 8–11. MERV 13 captures finer particles but may need a deeper filter cabinet to avoid restricting airflow. Check your system\'s specifications or ask a technician.'],
            ['question' => 'Do whole-home air purifiers really work?', 'answer' => 'Some technologies are well proven, such as high-efficiency media filtration and UV lights for coil surfaces. Others have less independent evidence. Ask the provider what specific problem a product addresses and how it is tested.'],
