        'group' => 'air',
        'icon' => 'wrench',
        'image' => 'technician-rooftop-equipment.jpg',
        'featured' => true,
        'short' => 'Seasonal tune-ups and preventive maintenance for air conditioners, furnaces, heat pumps, and ductless systems.',
        'hero_heading' => 'HVAC maintenance and tune-ups',
        'hero_text' => 'Regular maintenance helps your system run efficiently and catches small problems before they become breakdowns.',
        'overview' => '<p>Heating and cooling equipment works hardest at the start of each season — exactly when a neglected system is most likely to fail. A preventive maintenance visit cleans the parts that collect dirt, tests the parts that wear out, and checks the safety controls that protect your home.</p><p>Most manufacturers recommend annual professional service, and some equipment warranties require it. A common schedule is cooling service in spring and heating service in fall; heat pumps, which run year-round, benefit from both.</p>',
