        'details' => '<h2>What homeowners can do between visits</h2><ul><li>Check the filter monthly and replace it when dirty — every 1–3 months for most 1-inch filters.</li><li>Keep two feet of clearance around the outdoor unit and rinse off leaves and grass clippings.</li><li>Keep supply and return vents open and unblocked by furniture.</li><li>Pour a cup of diluted vinegar into the condensate line access in summer, if your system has one, to slow algae growth.</li><li>Test carbon monoxide alarms monthly.</li></ul>',
        'faqs' => [
            ['question' => 'How often should HVAC systems be serviced?', 'answer' => 'At least once a year. Ideally, schedule cooling service in spring and heating service in fall. Heat pumps and systems in harsh climates benefit from twice-yearly visits.'],
            ['question' => 'What is included in an HVAC tune-up?', 'answer' => 'Typical visits include cleaning coils and drains, checking refrigerant and electrical components, testing the thermostat and safety controls, and, for gas furnaces, combustion and venting checks. Ask the provider for a checklist of what their visit includes.'],
