        'seo_description' => 'Learn how residential heat pumps provide year-round heating and cooling, and connect with independent local HVAC service providers for heat pump installation, repair, and maintenance.',
        'overview' => '<p>A residential air-source heat pump is an all-in-one comfort system that cools your home in the summer and heats it in the winter. Instead of burning natural gas or generating heat solely with electric resistance coils, a heat pump uses a refrigerant cycle to transfer heat energy between the indoors and outdoors.</p><p>In cooling mode, it works just like a central air conditioner, absorbing heat from inside your house and releasing it outside. In heating mode, a component called a reversing valve changes the direction of refrigerant flow so the system extracts heat energy from the outdoor air—even in chilly weather—and brings it inside. HVAC Services connects homeowners with independent local contractors for heat pump installation, troubleshooting, and seasonal service.</p>',
